  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support to Convention on the prohibition of anti-personnel mines (APLC-ISU) 2026</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Verksamhetsst&#xf6;d till Ottawakonventionens enhet f&#xf6;r implementeringsst&#xf6;d 2026</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">F&#xf6;rekomsten av truppminor inneb&#xe4;r stora risker vad g&#xe4;ller s&#xe4;kerhet, h&#xe4;lsa och h&#xe5;llbar utveckling. Problematiken har s&#xe4;rskilt aktualiserats sedan Rysslands fullskaliga invasion av Ukraina d&#xe5; den omfattande kontamineringen av truppminor medf&#xf6;rt att Ukraina nu bed&#xf6;ms vara v&#xe4;rldens mest minkontaminerade land. Ett verksamhetsst&#xf6;d till Ottawakonventionens ISU bidrar p&#xe5; ett konkret s&#xe4;tt till att minska hotet fr&#xe5;n truppminor d&#xe5; ISU st&#xf6;djer statsparterna i genomf&#xf6;randet av konventionen.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The presence of anti-personnel landmines poses significant risks to security, health, and sustainable development. This issue has become particularly acute since Russia&#x2019;s full-scale invasion of Ukraine, as the extensive contamination by anti-personnel landmines has led to Ukraine now being assessed as the most mine-contaminated country in the world. Providing operational support to the Implementation Support Unit (ISU) of the Ottawa Convention makes a tangible contribution to reducing the threat posed by anti-personnel landmines, as the ISU supports States Parties in the implementation of the Convention.</narrative>
  </description>
